{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect","id":1422907,"title":"Best way to replicate Marvel Style Mutants ect?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-10T08:28:18-08:00","id":1422907,"title":"Best way to replicate Marvel Style Mutants ect?","content":"So I was wondering the big difference between comics and games about super heroes is that comics don\u2019t try to balance things some mutants are Omega level Full Quantum Franklin Richards some are Skin of Gen X and some are Marvel Girl who starts humble and becomes the Phoenix.<br /> <br /> So what is the best way to replicate a Marve style 616 Universe. Is it as simple as throwing out Quantum, or not having it restrict things, and allow Psi and Quantum Powers together? Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T08:56:28-08:00","id":1422909,"title":"","content":"I am fully expecting to see a Psychic Novas supplement in the Nexus. No, I don't have any special knowledge of such; but I'm still confident that one is on the way. What I mean by that is a book that adds Quantum powers and mega edges that replicate psionic powers that TC:Ab skipped. Given professor X and Jean Gray, such a book would be essential to using Aberrant to duplicate Marvel's X-Men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T08:59:48-08:00","id":1422911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1422909#post1422909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am fully expecting to see a Psychic Novas supplement in the Nexus. No, I don't have any special knowledge of such; but I'm still confident that one is on the way. What I mean by that is a book that adds Quantum powers and mega edges that replicate psionic powers that TC:Ab skipped. Given professor X and Jean Gray, such a book would be essential to using Aberrant to duplicate Marvel's X-Men.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are right on the money with that. Their is a want, nay a need, and the Market loves a Vacuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T09:26:40-08:00","id":1422914,"title":"","content":"As I see, the best (if not only) way to make all the X-men with a single set of rules is using Quantum powers. So I agree with Dataweaver.<br /> <br /> I have some notes on mental and precog powers for Novas, but it will take a while before we can publish anything for Aberrant in the Nexus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-10-2020, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T09:36:06-08:00","id":1422917,"title":"","content":"Well I am still trying to point out the issue that I want to discuss, in comics they don\u2019t worry about balance and Franklin Richards starts out with literal Create Universe Quantum powers. I want to embrace the disparate power levels rather then mandate everyone starts out low. This isn\u2019t necessarily true for PCs but for the setting it restricts things more in the direction of the author characters. They aren\u2019t Mary Sues but I am going to call them that so you get the jist. Meanwhile Comics are Dynamic and new characters can arrive on the scene and be world shakers, like when Legion showed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T09:51:58-08:00","id":1422918,"title":"","content":"Starting characters start somewhere between Quantum 1 and 5. That's a pretty big range. Most of your Marvel characters are going to fall somewhere in there, at least when they start their careers. You have a few outliers, but there is nothing in the book stopping you from having NPCs erupt at Quantum 7 or whatever. Just make sure they're supremely f-ed up at the same time to show why the PCs don't start that way. Honestly, Franklin Richards is basically a Quantum 10 nova. If you can create your own universe, you've transcended what it means to be human in anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T10:00:05-08:00","id":1422920,"title":"","content":"But I like things like Reed Richards who has top tier invention powers and low to mid tier stretch powers. Stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T10:14:50-08:00","id":1422921,"title":"","content":"Agree with Florin, Q1 to 5 is a pretty good measure of the power of almost any superhero we see in the comics, except maybe a few.<br /> <br /> Q2 Mutants are not the main cast of X-men, but most of the students are around here, with a few on Q1. My version of Spider-Man is a solid Q2, with some uses of maxing out once in a while.<br /> <br /> Most of the main cast of X-men are on Q3, including Cyclops, Colossus, Wolverine and Storm. What means they can fight Sentinels as equals (or almost as equals).<br /> <br /> I would put Magneto and Professor X on Q4, with some Maxing out and Qtech to improve their powers beyond that in a few situations. Iron Man armor must be around here too.<br /> <br /> Q5 Nova is pretty much Phoenix level in terms of raw power, maybe lacking the versatility Jean have if created as a new character. A Rank 5 Quantum Attack is almost a Nuke and can sink a Battleship with a few hits. I would put Hulk around here, probably Thor and Doc Strange.<br /> <br /> Beyond Q5 you can probably put a few more of the most famous heroes and villains, but it depends much on the writer to be honest.<br /> Franklin Richards I would consider a Q8 character with some moments of pure \u201cbeyond Q10\u201d lapses (like creating universes, something he did more than once but don\u2019t have a big impact in most of his stories.<br /> Galactus is a Q8 level creature that uses a rank 9 item to destroy worlds, but in general can destroy worlds with their own powers with some effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-10-2020, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T10:17:18-08:00","id":1422922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1422920#post1422920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I like things like Reed Richards who has top tier invention powers and low to mid tier stretch powers. Stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which should be easily modeled in the system. Most of his points will be spent on Q-Tech, Mega-Intelligence, and crafting powers, with a smaller amount of points put into his stretching power. You can have Q5 and 1 dot in a power, and it won't be extremely powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T11:09:26-08:00","id":1422924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1422909#post1422909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am fully expecting to see a Psychic Novas supplement in the Nexus. No, I don't have any special knowledge of such; but I'm still confident that one is on the way. What I mean by that is a book that adds Quantum powers and mega edges that replicate psionic powers that TC:Ab skipped. Given professor X and Jean Gray, such a book would be essential to using Aberrant to duplicate Marvel's X-Men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just gonna say I totally agree this, and would love to read something like this. So the moment it exists is the moment I go to the Nexus and buy it. Because it needs to be present, needs to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T11:26:47-08:00","id":1422927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1422921#post1422921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with Florin, Q1 to 5 is a pretty good measure of the power of almost any superhero we see in the comics, except maybe a few.<br /> <br /> Q2 Mutants are not the main cast of X-men, but most of the students are around here, with a few on Q1. My version of Spider-Man is a solid Q2, with some uses of maxing out once in a while.<br /> <br /> Most of the main cast of X-men are on Q3, including Cyclops, Colossus, Wolverine and Storm. What means they can fight Sentinels as equals (or almost as equals).<br /> <br /> I would put Magneto and Professor X on Q4, with some Maxing out and Qtech to improve their powers beyond that in a few situations. Iron Man armor must be around here too.<br /> <br /> Q5 Nova is pretty much Phoenix level in terms of raw power, maybe lacking the versatility Jean have if created as a new character. A Rank 5 Quantum Attack is almost a Nuke and can sink a Battleship with a few hits. I would put Hulk around here, probably Thor and Doc Strange.<br /> <br /> Beyond Q5 you can probably put a few more of the most famous heroes and villains, but it depends much on the writer to be honest.<br /> Franklin Richards I would consider a Q8 character with some moments of pure \u201cbeyond Q10\u201d lapses (like creating universes, something he did more than once but don\u2019t have a big impact in most of his stories.<br /> Galactus is a Q8 level creature that uses a rank 9 item to destroy worlds, but in general can destroy worlds with their own powers with some effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Spider-Man seems way more then Q2 he\u2019s taken on entire super teams by himself including the FF, Xmen, and Sinister Six. His agility and reflexes are top tier. Reed is also a multiversal intellect able to bridge Universes with his tech. Thor can Shatter mountains and when going all out can harm Celestials and Galactus.<br /> <br /> I see what you mean about putting them Q5 it gets the message across but it\u2019s not the same as an unwatered down version.<br /> <br /> Good writers like Hickman and Rick Remender make use of powers as being Unique and Transcendent in their own specialty like Cypher being seen generally week but he is godlike in his ability to communicate with beings like the Phalanx or Krakoa. Or when one person is needed for a specific thing like Goldballs unique power turning out being critical in Mutant resurrection or really out their powers like Moira McTaggert able to die and start her next life back in time with all the memories of the last timeline.<br /> <br /> How would I represent a being that goes Nova and is linked to all the versions of themselves in the Multiverse? Some powers don\u2019t work so well in the solidly defined system we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T12:08:44-08:00","id":1422932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1422927#post1422927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How would I represent a being that goes Nova and is linked to all the versions of themselves in the Multiverse? Some powers don\u2019t work so well in the solidly defined system we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use Mega-Intelligence and the Foresight, Instant Expert, and Mastermind mega-edges. Maybe some Mega-Presence and the Immediate Connection and Instant Influence mega-edges if knowing people from other timelines helps them with people in this one. I'd also look at the Prodigy mega-edge to utilize skill tricks they knew previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T12:09:49-08:00","id":1422933,"title":"","content":"One way to represent Spider-Man taking on the Fantastic Four is to allow Dramatic Editing for <i>everyone</i>, not just Talents; and when Spider-Man was able to keep up with the entire Fantastic Four, it was because their Inspiration reserves were depleted while his wasn't. <br /> <br /> Or, rephrased in an OOC way, Inspiration and Dramatic Editing were originally created to represent the narrative tropes in fiction where someone wins despite the odds being stacked against him. So if you're trying to supplicate the Marvel comics and their tendency for victors to be decided by what the plot needs instead of what the logic of their powers would dictate, them you should be relying on something akin to Inspiration and Dramatic Editing to reflect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T12:16:29-08:00","id":1422937,"title":"","content":"I mean the encounters make sense though. Spider-Man is insanely strong unless you have greater super strength, and he was swifter and more agile then Nightcrawler, who frankly isn\u2019t used to folks outclassing him. He bats above a mere Quantum two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T12:52:39-08:00","id":1422941,"title":"","content":"Spider man is not insanely strong. He can lift cars and break walls often, but he can't stop trains and lift boats all the time, it means he has Q2 and MM1, maxing out he can reach MM3 what is a lot (like lifting and throwing boat to the other side of the city).<br /> He is agile, but his agility is more related to dodging and acrobatics, and not much on doing things faster than usual or being infinitely precise, what I would put as MDex 2 and a set of Mega Edges (Defense, Accuracy, Prodigy on Athletics, and maybe a few more, possible Quantum Deflection).<br /> He can also do some super science, but not on Rich Richards (Q7 is enough to make any rank of Q-Tech) level or Tony Stark level (Q5 to build a Rank 7 if I am not wrong), it is more related to his Mega Cunning 2 with a few extra Mega Edges. He probably just have a high value of science and intelligence.<br /> <br /> Quantum is not about versatility in general, its more brute power, and Spider Man is not brute power. He is like a ninja, he can adapt and use what he have to deal with most problems, not like Goku that just Kamehameha the problems out of his way. Of course a higher Quantum is more effective on what they can do, but it doesn't means a lower quantum can't fight back.<br /> One example of Q3 is Cyclops, that can take the head of a Sentinel (Size 3 robot) with a single stare, and open holes in buildings (size 4 or 5) with some effort, or Wolverine that can recover from maimed condition in seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T13:05:59-08:00","id":1422944,"title":"","content":"Don't forget his web slingers. That's definitely q tech. Not particularly powerful q tech, but q tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T13:13:25-08:00","id":1422946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1422944#post1422944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget his web slingers. That's definitely q tech. Not particularly powerful q tech, but q tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Websligers are his master craft work that he is always reworking. I would make it a ran 5 Qtech with a set of quantum attacks (entangle, web bomb and web ball) and the Swing Movement Mode","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T20:11:33-08:00","id":1423017,"title":"","content":"Answering the OP question: whine a lot about being feared and hated while still having to protect humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T02:24:47-08:00","id":1423031,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t really have anything new to say, but I love X-Men stuff and I really Like this question. I do think you can simulate characters like Professor X and Jean Grey using just quantum powers (you don\u2019t need to give them psi for the setting to work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:10:50-08:00","id":1423058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1423017#post1423017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answering the OP question: whine a lot about being feared and hated while still having to protect humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hoho<br /> <br /> <br /> What about other hard to replicate because they are game breaking powers? Like rogues it would be fun for an NPC to have her power. Maybe give you insanity of dual identity until you buy off with Exp the new power if you permanently stole it.<br /> <br /> Or mimic able to mimic five different super power templates at half strength I guess I would treat it as a level lower or with increased difficulty depending on the powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:24:49-08:00","id":1423061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1423031#post1423031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really have anything new to say, but I love X-Men stuff and I really Like this question. I do think you can simulate characters like Professor X and Jean Grey using just quantum powers (you don\u2019t need to give them psi for the setting to work).</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading someone's mind falls under the Psi Aptitude, Telepathy. Full stop. So does directly controlling someone's mind. Or erasing their memories. Now, maybe you can kinda/sorta/not-exactly kludge some of those effects through Quantum abilities and Mega-Edges, but if you want to do what Jean Grey and especially Professor X do, you need Psi powers. Jean Grey would be a very powerful Psiad with Primary Aptitudes in Telepathy and Psychokinesis. Professor X would be a &quot;natural Psion&quot; with the Aptitude Mode, Telepathy and Proxy-level powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:31:34-08:00","id":1423062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1423058#post1423058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about other hard to replicate because they are game breaking powers? Like rogues it would be fun for an NPC to have her power. Maybe give you insanity of dual identity until you buy off with Exp the new power if you permanently stole it.<br /> <br /> Or mimic able to mimic five different super power templates at half strength I guess I would treat it as a level lower or with increased difficulty depending on the powers</div> </div> </div> </div>Quantum Imprint is the power for that. Rogue has only really permanently drained a few people. So, her normal method of using her powers would use Quantum Imprint with the Extra Power (bought multiple times) and Theft tags. Mimic would also use Quantum Imprint with copious use of the Extra Power tag. You could do his half-power restriction as either some kind of negative power tag or else just be keeping his dots in Quantum Imprint low, since that sets a cap on the number of dots you can mimic in a power.<br /> <br /> ETA: Rogue and Mimic might not need quite as many Extra Power tags as I thought. Power suites count as one power. So, you can steal/copy a whole power suite without using the Extra Power tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":". 11-11-2020, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T09:06:36-08:00","id":1423069,"title":"","content":"Cool how permanent is that though?<br /> <br /> I am glad they are versatile in Aberrant. I need to read it thoroughly now that it is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T10:09:54-08:00","id":1423074,"title":"","content":"Depends how many power tags you want to throw on it. The base is Quantum + Quantum Imprint rounds. If you add Duration power tags to it, you can get it up to Quantum + Quantum Imprint days. You can always re-up the duration by spending the activation cost again at the end of the duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T17:58:57-08:00","id":1423151,"title":"","content":"I'd argue the three paths are broken up in X-men. Domino and and Longshot are clearly running on Talent or maybe higher level Paramorph tricks(as Might Scarlet witch!). Professor x doesn't rock megattributes and there seems to be a whole setup for psychics and psychics alone in x-men comics that others really don't play with. THE only character I think really requires multiple types of Mechanics.. might be... Legion? But his powers are all over the place.<br /> <br /> You just replace Inspiration with the x-gene and you've pretty much go it in one. Now if you want some sort of commonality of X powers in a universe where the Increadible Hulk and Thor exist that's going to be a lot harder to pull off with the continuum as presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T18:06:47-08:00","id":1423154,"title":"","content":"Once again, I should point out the Trinity Continuum isn't <i>trying</i> to be a generic superheroes game, any more than Exalted is generic D&amp;D fantasy. You're going to have to stretch concepts to fit, if you want to keep the setting. And if you want to change the setting to fit the concepts, that's the realm of house rules. Which means if you want pure-Aberrant X-men, they don't have psychic powers, they have various Mega-Int stuff that does the &quot;my theory of mind is sophisticated enough to simulate another person's thought to a high degree of accuracy&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> As it is, it's probably not incredibly broken in context to simply dispose of the &quot;you can only be a Nova, a Psion/ad, or a Talent&quot; restriction and to either unify the power stats or allow someone to have multiple and track them seperately. I'd probably keep the 'different branches of powers interfere with each other' thing from mainline TC since directly <i>combining</i> Nova powers and Psi stuff (let alone Dramatic Editing and Gifts) isn't something the system was ever tested to do, but hey, why not try it and see what blows up? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Does mean you need to buy the other books, but I was doing that anyway so no skin off <i>my</i> nose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T19:03:15-08:00","id":1423161,"title":"","content":"But i honestly can't think of a character who wouldn't slot one side or the other? Maybe Shatterstar? Legion? Most Mutants fall into &quot;Luck/probabiliy manipulators&quot; &quot;Psychics&quot; and Supers. I mean there's even treated as some difference the firestarting ability of Jean Grey and the fire starting ability of Pyro. The Stepford cookoos even show the whole unified psychic powers that you can't get from nova powers period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T20:26:24-08:00","id":1423170,"title":"","content":"Doctor Strange being a Sorcerer doesn't quite fit the bill for being just one type.<br /> <br /> Onslaught was kind of all over the place but I guess that is just God level Psi, even with Magneto's power tossed in. Proteus had Psionic Powers and Reality powers so that is kind of too gonzo for Psi unless we see some Psi 10 stuff its more Psi and Quantum.<br /> <br /> I guess for things like Miora's reincarnation power you could just use a plot device power and not worry about it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T20:29:22-08:00","id":1423171,"title":"","content":"My point in put every mutant in the same bag is not about Quantum itself, but to have a single set of rules that cover all mutations, so Rogue can drain any of them following same rules.<br /> <br /> I would make it another \u201csource\u201d calling Quantum as X-Gene, or what ever. Other heroes would have other rule sets, maybe Asgardians follow something closer to psi, except for the higher scale in general, and \u201cnormal humans\u201d like Tony Stark work closer to Talents but with some access to Novatech creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T21:00:33-08:00","id":1423176,"title":"","content":"I really would like to have at some point in a game some folks from another Universe who don't follow the Quantum/Flux/Psi Paradigm so this is an interesting discussion.<br /> <br /> How necessary is a Power Trait? It works for some like say Asgardians, or some Godlike Omega level mutants and Psychics, or even folks like Magneto who clearly improved over their lifetime.<br /> <br /> But others don't really have some powerful lifeforce like trait, though I guess someone like Wolverine could use say a Talent Template with a few slapped on powers as he mostly works on improving his skills rather then powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T04:44:53-08:00","id":1423238,"title":"","content":"One thing most superheroes have, and all Mutants have for sure, is a defined scope of powers and a \u201ckind of\u201d described power level. While Aberrant and most RPGs is all about personal advance and evolving powers. They are a bit incompatible, even more if you think a Nova will suddenly gain a new transformation. There are exceptions (The Beast is there to show) but they are usually related to external sources, not about genetics going nuts.<br /> <br /> That said, a power trait is a tangible thing we see in many situations, we try to classify characters and eventually the writers create an scale for that. The mutant levels for example fit awesomely well to quantum levels, a level 5 mutant (Jean) has an entire scale of power above a level 4 mutant (Magneto), and most of the X-man are level 3 mutants.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s not just that, you must define in game rules how the things work, if you don\u2019t have a power trait you don\u2019t have a proper energy consumption defined (that\u2019s basically the main need for a quantum trait) or a uneven character, almost unplayable, with a trait as high as possible and nothing else. Superiors are an exception, first because they don\u2019t use Energy, second because they have a power cap reachable from starting level, they CAN reach their maximum level in several powers at same time from char gen, basically they all have Quantum 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T13:30:35-08:00","id":1423355,"title":"","content":"Technically, they don't. Quantum 1 is incompatible with Psi 1, and Superiors have Psi 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T15:18:06-08:00","id":1423388,"title":"","content":"Short answer? You can't replicate X-men comics in Aberrant. Aberrant tries to &quot;simulate power levels&quot; where X-Men is &quot;narrative power levels&quot;. You can basically make X-men using more narrative focused games like Fate, Masks, Words In Peril, Marvel Heroic Roleplaying (or the Cortex Prime version that is coming).<br /> <br /> I am not saying you can't create characters with some of their powers, but many unique things that exists in X-Men and similar comics are either impossible without house-rules or you must spend so much points to make it similar that the characters would have big differences in XP to spend. These other games I cited are best for doing comics, Aberrant is RPG of superpowered characters, not RPG for simulating comics logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T15:26:30-08:00","id":1423391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1423061#post1423061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading someone's mind falls under the Psi Aptitude, Telepathy. Full stop. So does directly controlling someone's mind. Or erasing their memories. Now, maybe you can kinda/sorta/not-exactly kludge some of those effects through Quantum abilities and Mega-Edges, but if you want to do what Jean Grey and especially Professor X do, you need Psi powers. Jean Grey would be a very powerful Psiad with Primary Aptitudes in Telepathy and Psychokinesis. Professor X would be a &quot;natural Psion&quot; with the Aptitude Mode, Telepathy and Proxy-level powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works too. You could always create your own Quantum powers to simulate Jean Grey\u2019s and Professor X\u2019s abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-12-2020, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T16:28:25-08:00","id":1423407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422907-best-way-to-replicate-marvel-style-mutants-ect?p=1423355#post1423355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, they don't. Quantum 1 is incompatible with Psi 1, and Superiors have Psi 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is more like, they all have the power trait at same level. But you got me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}